      "identification": "Universal Mach-O password and wallet stealer masquerading as Installer",
      "execution": "ARM64 main at 0x100000690 constructs a string at 0x1000006ac, obtains its C string at 0x1000006b4, and calls system at 0x1000006b8. crypt<37077> starts at 0x1000007dc. The source pointer is ARM64 file offset 0x14de0; identical ciphertext is also present at 0x4c90 in x86-64. Each byte XORs the low state byte; state starts at 0x11667 and updates as ((state * 0x3785) & 0xffffffff) % 35999. Recovered source starts with osascript -e and evaluates return-joined AppleScript.",
      "effects": [
        "Fake Installation dialog obtains a hidden password and checks it with dscl authonly; .pwd caches credentials.",
        "Copies Chromium and Gecko credential/cookie databases, wallet extension and desktop-wallet stores, Keychain databases, Notes databases/media and extension-filtered Desktop/Documents files into random /tmp staging. Finder copying is a protected-store access path; Notes scripting is a fallback.",
        "Collects system_profiler hardware/software/display output; ditto archives staging into /tmp/out.zip and curl POSTs it to configured host charge0x.at. Removes staging and ZIP afterward.",
        "Downloads replacement Ledger Live contents, terminates the original app, uses the captured password with sudo to remove it, and extracts the replacement into Applications.",
        "Downloads shell command text, inserts it into bash -c ProgramArguments, writes/copies a RunAtLoad/KeepAlive LaunchDaemon, and requests launchctl bootstrap. nohup is the fallback."
      ],
      "limits": [
